        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Use 300 to 500 miles as a prompt, not a deadline, and replace
            running shoes when the cushioning feels flat or your legs start to complain.</strong>
            For a runner on 15 miles a week that is roughly every five to eight months; on a
            treadmill, ignore the clean outsole and go by miles and feel.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Note the start date of each pair, keep a running total, rotate two pairs if you run often,
